§ `s 10(13) extension so that special benefits may be paid up to the maximum total (src:296-300, 315)`
-- Maxima in s 12(3): pregnancy 15; parental 35 or 61 by election; sickness 26; compassionate care 26.
`ei1 test pregnancy 15 weeks` MEANS `ei1 Special benefits paid for one reason` OF `pregnancy`, 15
`ei1 test parental 40 weeks` MEANS `ei1 Special benefits paid for one reason` OF `caring for a new-born or adopted child`, 40
`ei1 test parental 61 weeks` MEANS `ei1 Special benefits paid for one reason` OF `caring for a new-born or adopted child`, 61
`ei1 test parental 20 weeks` MEANS `ei1 Special benefits paid for one reason` OF `caring for a new-born or adopted child`, 20
`ei1 test parental 0 weeks` MEANS `ei1 Special benefits paid for one reason` OF `caring for a new-born or adopted child`, 0
`ei1 test sickness 20 weeks` MEANS `ei1 Special benefits paid for one reason` OF `a prescribed illness, injury or quarantine`, 20
`ei1 test sickness 26 weeks` MEANS `ei1 Special benefits paid for one reason` OF `a prescribed illness, injury or quarantine`, 26
`ei1 test family member 26 weeks` MEANS `ei1 Special benefits paid for one reason` OF `care or support of a family member`, 26
#ASSERT `s 10(13) the maximum number of weeks established for the reason for which special benefits were paid` `ei1 test pregnancy 15 weeks` `the 61-week maximum` EQUALS 15
#ASSERT `s 10(13) the maximum number of weeks established for the reason for which special benefits were paid` `ei1 test parental 40 weeks` `the 61-week maximum` EQUALS 61
#ASSERT `s 10(13) the maximum number of weeks established for the reason for which special benefits were paid` `ei1 test parental 40 weeks` `the 35-week maximum` EQUALS 35
#ASSERT `s 10(13)(c) the maximum total number of weeks established for the reasons for which special benefits were paid` (LIST `ei1 test pregnancy 15 weeks`, `ei1 test parental 40 weeks`) `the 61-week maximum` EQUALS 76
#ASSERT `s 10(13)(c) the maximum total number of weeks established for the reasons for which special benefits were paid` (LIST `ei1 test pregnancy 15 weeks`, `ei1 test parental 40 weeks`) `the 35-week maximum` EQUALS 50
#ASSERT `s 10(13)(c) the maximum total number of weeks established for the reasons for which special benefits were paid` (LIST `ei1 test pregnancy 15 weeks`, `ei1 test parental 0 weeks`) `the 61-week maximum` EQUALS 15
-- args: regular benefits were paid, the special benefits paid, the election
-- 15 + 61 = 76 is more than 50, and the parental benefits were paid for 40 weeks, fewer than 61: extended.
#ASSERT `s 10(13) the benefit period is extended so that special benefits may be paid up to the maximum total number of weeks` FALSE (LIST `ei1 test pregnancy 15 weeks`, `ei1 test parental 40 weeks`) `the 61-week maximum`
-- 15 + 35 = 50 is not more than 50.
#ASSERT NOT (`s 10(13) the benefit period is extended so that special benefits may be paid up to the maximum total number of weeks` FALSE (LIST `ei1 test pregnancy 15 weeks`, `ei1 test parental 20 weeks`) `the 35-week maximum`)
-- regular benefits were paid: not extended under (13)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 10(13) the benefit period is extended so that special benefits may be paid up to the maximum total number of weeks` TRUE (LIST `ei1 test pregnancy 15 weeks`, `ei1 test parental 40 weeks`) `the 61-week maximum`)
-- only one reason: not extended
#ASSERT NOT (`s 10(13) the benefit period is extended so that special benefits may be paid up to the maximum total number of weeks` FALSE (LIST `ei1 test parental 40 weeks`) `the 61-week maximum`)
-- a reason with no weeks paid is not a reason for which benefits were paid
#ASSERT NOT (`s 10(13) the benefit period is extended so that special benefits may be paid up to the maximum total number of weeks` FALSE (LIST `ei1 test pregnancy 15 weeks`, `ei1 test parental 0 weeks`) `the 61-week maximum`)
-- every benefit paid for its full maximum: paragraph (b) fails
#ASSERT NOT (`s 10(13) the benefit period is extended so that special benefits may be paid up to the maximum total number of weeks` FALSE (LIST `ei1 test pregnancy 15 weeks`, `ei1 test parental 61 weeks`) `the 61-week maximum`)
-- the length (15) calculates: 2 + 76 = 78; 2 + 15 + 61 + 26 = 104 exactly; more is cut at 104 by subsection (14)
#ASSERT `s 10(15) the maximum number of weeks in a benefit period extended under subsection (13)` (LIST `ei1 test pregnancy 15 weeks`, `ei1 test parental 40 weeks`) `the 61-week maximum` EQUALS 78
#ASSERT `s 10(15) the maximum number of weeks in a benefit period extended under subsection (13)` (LIST `ei1 test pregnancy 15 weeks`, `ei1 test parental 40 weeks`, `ei1 test sickness 20 weeks`) `the 61-week maximum` EQUALS 104
#ASSERT `s 10(15) the maximum number of weeks in a benefit period extended under subsection (13)` (LIST `ei1 test pregnancy 15 weeks`, `ei1 test parental 40 weeks`, `ei1 test sickness 20 weeks`, `ei1 test family member 26 weeks`) `the 61-week maximum` EQUALS 104
-- the extension: 78 - 52 = 26; 104 - 52 = 52; none when the conditions fail
#ASSERT `s 10(13) the number of weeks by which the benefit period is extended` FALSE (LIST `ei1 test pregnancy 15 weeks`, `ei1 test parental 40 weeks`) `the 61-week maximum` EQUALS 26
#ASSERT `s 10(13) the number of weeks by which the benefit period is extended` FALSE (LIST `ei1 test pregnancy 15 weeks`, `ei1 test parental 40 weeks`, `ei1 test sickness 20 weeks`) `the 61-week maximum` EQUALS 52
#ASSERT `s 10(13) the number of weeks by which the benefit period is extended` TRUE (LIST `ei1 test pregnancy 15 weeks`, `ei1 test parental 40 weeks`) `the 61-week maximum` EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `s 10(13) the number of weeks by which the benefit period is extended` FALSE (LIST `ei1 test pregnancy 15 weeks`, `ei1 test parental 20 weeks`) `the 35-week maximum` EQUALS 0

